e":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"098a13d3e8f939dd8a2be8707883d1e20dcdad8b26f80c9f5e583db89dc30a04","event_uuid":"3078586c-181f-4e72-8224-9dd13a3083f8","position":{"commit_sha":"b9a6e77edf716247318b3b9dac1aa7f557cf4b6a","position":"1788359911435984806-3078586c-181f-4e72-8224-9dd13a3083f8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bfb03e2f265fb24f159ebe27c8be62de99d29e78ef8a00ad04a09f78d874a55d","event_uuid":"5ecbcd85-b393-4c92-b05b-34f84c03900a","position":{"commit_sha":"d7c7f8df7599070d85665ac2402e50e9d2a46026","position":"1788362788132418001-5ecbcd85-b393-4c92-b05b-34f84c03900a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"507d82b307cac39d49ede99f77af65899580dbf328572fe93f31465c905933b8","event_uuid":"c6253af1-5ded-4bdc-9547-b4fcd2cc07a7","position":{"commit_sha":"5ba5e3363a6defc1190a0decd3f45ddbabe88807","position":"1788362807346810001-c6253af1-5ded-4bdc-9547-b4fcd2cc07a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788311519832908570,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a3257956-52aa-4746-9e3c-283655cc2c1d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"468c-d64e-94d5-4f31"},{"link_uuid":"01bfa3c7-041a-46b0-9a47-edb31d35598b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3a03-5d80-eeb9-4d4e"},{"link_uuid":"3078586c-181f-4e72-8224-9dd13a3083f8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"974d-a242-1849-4ff0"}],"description":"## Context\n\nTest isolation under ~90-worktree/xdist parallelism is 15.8% of the defect stream (R2S1). The harness root already exists and propagates: `tests/conftest.py:486-513` provides the session-scoped `_rebar_root_sandbox_repo` and an autouse fixture that `monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_ROOT\", ...)`, per-worker under xdist via `tmp_path_factory`. Propagation to children is by **environment inheritance**, so a test that builds its own `env=` dict from scratch silently drops `REBAR_ROOT` and the child falls back to the git toplevel of cwd — the real checkout.\n\nWhat is missing is ENFORCEMENT: nothing stops a new unit-tier test from spawning a subprocess with its own ad-hoc temp/HOME/root, which is how the recent class instances arose (`82a0d5cd`: a `home=Path.home()` default reached transitively, resolving the operator's real home; `ef9e1d74`: a single subprocess wall-clock bound conflating a product deadline with machine slack). Precedent: pip's `pytest_collection_modifyitems` raising on forbidden patterns; Bazel's hermetic `TEST_TMPDIR` contract (12c) recorded as the escalation path.\n\n## Approach\n\nA fourth arm in the existing `pytest_collection_modifyitems` (`tests/conftest.py:220`), delegating to a **pure predicate** in a new `tests/_subprocess_isolation.py` — mirroring the `_live_jira_confinement` split, so the predicate is unit-testable without spawning pytest.\n\nDetection is **AST, not regex**: resolve `ast.Call` sites whose callee binds to `subprocess.{run,Popen,check_output,check_call,call}`, `os.system`, `os.popen`, or `pytest.main`, resolving module aliases from the file's own imports. Regex is disqualified — a naive `run(` pattern matches 126 `asyncio.run` sites.\n\nThe census on the current tier is 866 spawn sites across 334 files, of which ~841 already take their root from the harness (`cwd=<fixture path>`, `git -C <fixture path>`, a positional `git init <tmp_path>`, `env=subprocess_env(...)`, or plain env inheritance). Only ~26 are hazards, in three shapes: an `env=` dict literal carrying neither `os.environ` nor `REBAR_ROOT` (3), `cwd=REPO_ROOT`/`git -C REPO_ROOT` (23), and one site reading the operator's `$HOME`.\n\n**Bounding the check conservatively is a requirement, not a nicety.** Roughly 58 sites pass `env=<bare variable>` and are undecidable without a def-site trace; these are REPORTED, never failed — failing them would redden 42 files on day one. The sanctioned nested-pytest funnel `tests/_nested_pytest.py` and its four documented exceptions are exempt by name.\n\nFailures raise `pytest.UsageError`, not `pytest.fail`: this arm can fire from the xdist controller, where a `pytest.fail` escapes as a 20-line `INTERNALERROR>` traceback — the precedent and its rationale are already recorded at `tests/conftest.py:264-274` (\"a guard whose whole value is a clear message must not look like a crash\").\n\nThe opt-out is `@pytest.mark.allow_unharnessed_subprocess(\"<reason>\")`. `--strict-markers` validates only the marker NAME, so the mandatory-reason rule is enforced by the guard itself (empty/blank args fail collection) — the same \"reason is mandatory\" convention as `# read-via:` in `check_config_reads.py`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: collection fails with an instructive error naming the fixture to use, when a unit-tier test spawns a subprocess without taking its root from the harness. Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py`, which drives the predicate over a seeded violation fixture.\n- [x] AC2: the full unit tier collects clean at introduction, with the ~26 hazard sites fixed or explicitly marked and no blanket opt-out. Verified by `pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit` exiting 0.\n- [x] AC3: the guard raises `pytest.UsageError` (not `pytest.fail`) so an xdist-controller failure reads as a clean `ERROR:` banner. Verified by a test asserting the raised type.\n- [x] AC4: the opt-out marker requires a non-blank reason string, and a bare or empty-reason marker fails collection. Verified by a test over both forms.\n- [x] AC5: opt-out growth is greppable and countable, so the mechanism ratchet can see it. Verified by `grep -rn \"allow_unharnessed_subprocess\" tests/ | wc -l` returning the marked-site count.\n- [x] AC6: statically undecidable `env=<bare variable>` sites are reported, not failed. Verified by a test asserting such a site yields a report entry and no collection failure.\n- [x] AC7: the check and the marker are documented alongside the existing isolation helpers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py -v` — the guard's own suite: seeded violation fires (AC1), `UsageError` type (AC3), marker reason required (AC4), undecidable site reported not failed (AC6). The predicate is exercised directly, so no nested pytest spawn is needed.\n- `pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit` — proves the tier collects clean at introduction (AC2).\n- `pytest -n 4 --collect-only -q tests/unit` — proves the controller path renders the message cleanly rather than as an INTERNALERROR (AC3).\n- `grep -rn \"allow_unharnessed_subprocess\" tests/ | wc -l` — the countable opt-out census (AC5).\n- `make lint && make typecheck` — house gates stay green.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `tests/_subprocess_isolation.py` (new; the pure AST predicate, unit-testable in isolation)\n- `tests/conftest.py` (fourth arm in `pytest_collection_modifyitems`; register the marker in `pytest_configure`)\n- `tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py` (new; seeded-violation RED proof and the marker/undecidable cases)\n- the ~26 hazard sites fixed or marked (final set from the AST census)\n- `docs/` (the testing/isolation section documenting the existing guards)","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/conftest.py","reason":"collection-time guard hook"},{"path":"tests/_isolation.py","reason":"detection logic home (or new tests/_collection_guards.py)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py","reason":"seeded-violation RED proof"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","87cb-7121-a3b6-4606"],["relates_to","3a03-5d80-eeb9-4d4e"],["relates_to","468c-d64e-94d5-4f31"],["relates_to","974d-a242-1849-4ff0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","parent_status_uuid":"5ecbcd85-b393-4c92-b05b-34f84c03900a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"15f2-f3d4-ffcd-4223","ticket_type":"story","title":"Collection-time enforcement: unit-tier subprocess tests must take isolation roots from the harness","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4a8faed2-7eb2-4ebc-be17-9fb1025930c7","62741525-9478-4a93-bc8e-4fbe3943524c","c2c80e43-d7a2-4c11-aad9-fe635b9d8a4c","9f0c9048-5f0b-4fad-bde7-dcc526075998","5eb34004-1ffd-4a3b-a855-d9456acb277e","0bb7d5a6-a0bf-42bf-b19b-45be31f41594","a3257956-52aa-4746-9e3c-283655cc2c1d","01bfa3c7-041a-46b0-9a47-edb31d35598b","62379511-2e77-42cf-9479-da9980c7e4fb","3078586c-181f-4e72-8224-9dd13a3083f8","5ecbcd85-b393-4c92-b05b-34f84c03900a","c6253af1-5ded-4bdc-9547-b4fcd2cc07a7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788373020992073891,"uuid":"05873b1d-e7a2-4c65-97f8-c38f1f9092d9"}